  "storedNote": "The core keeps a conversation's last message, a quote and a search hit as a stored token, not display text: `{\"k\":\"im.preview.<kind>\",\"a\":{…}}` (flare-im-core-sdk `src/content/preview_storage.rs`, written by `elem_preview_storage_payload`). `stored` lists tokens exactly as the core serializes them — an empty `a` is left out, so a picture without a caption is `{\"k\":\"im.preview.image\"}` — and what each reads as. Vue implements it in `displayTextFromStoredPreview`, the native kits in `flareStoredPreviewText`; every platform's test reads this list. A token's own words win (a caption, a file name, a title, the server's `fb` for a system line); the rest read as their `preview*` term, a system line without words by the kit's `systemEvent.<ek>` label for its event key, else `preview.system`. The event keys are the `SystemContent.event_kind` values the social server writes (flare-social `system_event_kind.rs`); an event whose label includes a name reads it from the token's parameters (`p.display_name`, else `p.name`) and says the event without it when they carry none. Text that is not a token is history from before the tokens and reads as it is; a token the kit does not know, or one with no words where words are the whole message, reads as nothing — never its raw JSON. Markdown is read as plain text and pack keys as their names, as in `cases`.",
